 html←RenderReadme(markdown sourceUrl prefix);parms;lines;removed;group;repo;tag;ns
⍝ Turns a package's README into HTML fit to be dropped into a package page, as a vector of
⍝ character vectors like everything else that builds a page here.
⍝ ⍵ is the Markdown as stored, the URL it was fetched from, and a prefix that keeps its ids
⍝ from colliding with the page's own.
⍝ The order is the point of this function:
⍝ 1. every HTML tag goes before MarkAPL ever sees the text. A README is somebody else's
⍝    writing on somebody else's server, so it is treated as text and nothing else: <script>,
⍝    <iframe>, "onclick=" and the rest never arise, because no HTML survives to carry them.
⍝    `RemoveHtmlTags` is what group home pages already use for exactly this reason.
⍝ 2. MarkAPL renders what is left, so every tag in the result is one we generated
⍝ 3. only then are headings, ids and links adjusted, and by then it is our own HTML
⍝ Returns '' when there is nothing worth showing, which the caller should take as "leave the
⍝ section out altogether" rather than "print an empty heading".
 html←''
 :If 0=≢markdown
     :Return
 :EndIf
⍝ Stored by ⎕NPUT and read back by ⎕NGET, so the line endings are LFs by now, while
⍝ `RemoveHtmlTags` and `MassageMarkdown` both work in CRLFs.
 markdown←(⎕UCS 10)⎕R CRLF⊣markdown~⎕UCS 13
 (markdown removed)←RemoveHtmlTags markdown
 :If 0=≢lines←MassageMarkdown markdown
     :Return
 :EndIf
 parms←##.MarkAPL.CreateParms
 parms.createFullHtmlPage←0                         ⍝ A fragment: the page brings its own <head>
 parms.verbose←0
 parms.ignoreEmbeddedParms←1                        ⍝ A README must not configure our renderer
 parms.bookmarkLink←0                               ⍝ No paragraph markers on somebody else's headings
 parms.javaScript←0                                 ⍝ The page has its own; none is wanted from here
 parms.copy2ClipboardBtn←0
 parms.checkLinks←0                                 ⍝ Broken links in a README are not our business
 parms.toc←0
 (html ns)←parms ##.MarkAPL.Markdown2HTML lines
 html←DemoteHeadings html
 html←prefix PrefixReadmeIds html
 (group repo tag)←ParseReadmeSourceUrl sourceUrl
 html←(group repo tag)ResolveReadmeLinks html
⍝Done
